  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\nIssued at 150 PM CST TUE NOV 10 2026\n\nThis afternoon at the surface, ridging is present over the Gulf\nCoast with weak flow across Alabama. In the upper levels, we have\nSW flow into C AL out of a shortwave currently over TX. This is \nresulting in some scattered mid to upper clouds. However, the \nlower levels are too dry for any precipitation across our area. \nThis will change on Wed. The latest guidance weakens the shortwave\nas it moves toward AL, but there is still a small chance of a \nlight shower during the day ahead of the main surface front. As \nthe front gets closer Wed night, chances of rain occurrence will \nincrease. However, heavy rain and thunderstorms are not \nanticipated, and QPF amounts will be low overall. Behind the \nfront, northwest winds will increase with a much colder airmass \nmoving S/SEWD behind it. A 1024 to 1028mb ridge pushes SWD out of \nCentral Canada Thu into the Plains and Midwest. With this intrusion\nof colder air, a medium chance of frost is expected for early Fri\nmorning. Even colder air is expected for Sat/Sun morning with a \nmedium chance of freezing temperatures and a high probability of \nwidespread frost. Temperatures should begin to moderate a little \nfor Mon/Tue as the surface ridge center shifts EWD across E Conus,\nbut frost will still remain a medium probability for those mornings.\n\n08",
